<task>
1. Go through the list of tags above and, for each tag, make an informal non-xml list of any events in the text that would quality. If unsure if something is an event, include it. In some cases, events must be *inferred* from the text rather than explicitly stated. In those cases, annotate your XML for that inference with a note in <!-- XML comment --> format with a sentence or two explaining the inference and the text that supports it. The ultimate purpose of event extraction is to keep the game state up to date with the prose.

2. For any events that you listed more than once, determine which is the best fit. Err on the side of keeping events rather than omitting them entirely; just remove duplicates.

3. In text format, list each tracker by name along with its current value and no more than 10 words about whether it needs to be updated based on the text. Countdown trackers already display remaining time; do not update them just because time passed. Update them only if the deadline changes or the countdown target is reached/resolved.

3. Output only one `<events>...</events>` XML block containing the best fitting events in chronological order. Do not include commentary, markdown fences, or any text outside the XML block.
</task>
